	abstract = {State-of-the-art remote sensing technique has been playing an important role in grassland science research, and its application in grassland resource monitoring and management has been continuously strengthened. This paper reviewed the positioning and theoretical framework of remote sensing observation technique in the research of grassland resource monitoring and management. We recapitulated the development of satellite remote sensing observation systems and rendered a general conception of grassland remote sensing applications. Thereafter, we retrospected the progress and achievements of remote sensing techniques in grassland resource survey, accurate identification of grassland species, inversion of grassland productivity, grassland vegetation carbon cycle, grassland phenology monitoring, grassland biodiversity identification, as well as the unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV)-driven applications and remote sensing-related decision-making management (DMM) over the past five decades. Some issues on remote sensing applications in the monitoring and management of grassland resources were presented and discussed. Finally, concerning the ongoing development of grassland remote sensing techniques in the new era, it was pointed out that establishing a three-dimensional monitoring network from satellite-UAV-based to fixed-site ground-truth syncing observations was the key to the in-deep and extensive application of grassland remote sensing technique. © 2022 Editorial Department of Chinese Journal of Grassland. All rights reserved.},
